# Template. The real file lives only on the host at /opt/dawarich/.env
# (root:root, 0640) and is gitignored -- nothing in this repo deploys this one.
#
# Both are left empty on purpose. compose.yaml reads them as ${VAR:?...},
# and the `:?` form errors on empty as well as unset -- so copying this file
# verbatim stops the stack with a clear message instead of starting it on a
# credential that is published in this repo. Which is the failure this stack
# was found in: see stacks/dawarich/README.md.
#
# The README has a one-liner that generates both.
#
# Reverse geocoding is not configured on this stack and needs no key here --
# see the README's Reverse geocoding section for what it would take.

# Signs and encrypts the Rails session cookie. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 64
#
# The upstream compose file defaults this to the literal string CHANGE_ME.
# Anyone who has read that file -- it is the first result for "dawarich docker
# compose" -- can then forge a session cookie for any account on the instance,
# with no password. Treat a leak of this value as a full account compromise and
# rotate it; the only cost is that everyone signs in again.
#
# It is also the seed for the ActiveRecord encryption keys, unless the
# OTP_ENCRYPTION_* trio is set explicitly. Nothing is encrypted with them today
# because no account has 2FA enabled -- once one does, rotating this line
# invalidates that enrolment, so set those three first.
SECRET_KEY_BASE=

# Password for the bundled PostGIS. Never leaves the compose network -- the
# database publishes no port -- but the app, the worker and the database all
# authenticate with it. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Hex on purpose: this value is not URL-encoded anywhere it is used, and
# choosing a charset that cannot need escaping is cheaper than checking.
#
# Read at initdb time only. On a host whose cluster already exists, changing
# this line gives you an app that cannot log in, not a rotated password. Change
# it in the database too -- see the README.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
